// Q-044 `quillo check` lets `n / 4` (always a float) through where a builtin takes an int: an error only at run time
// mode: check
// open-when: /ok \(0 routes/
// fixed-when: expects an int
// From FEEDBACK4.md (found on 5d2e21e). In the bank's lib/iban.qwe, grouping an account number
// in fours: `range(0, (len(c) + 3) / 4)`. `/` of two ints is a float in Quillo; `range` takes
// ints; the program stopped at run time. `floor(...)` fixed it.

fn groups(s: str) -> list = range(0, (len(s) + 3) / 4)

print(range(0, 7 / 2))
